  E'Reproducible random numbers',
  E'Two Sigma''s research review board will reject a backtest that can''t be reproduced bit-for-bit. Every random draw in a research notebook gets a seed — usually a module-level constant, sometimes per-experiment. Reproducibility is non-negotiable.',
  E'Seed two generators with the same value and confirm they produce identical draws.',
  E'**Concept.** `np.random.default_rng(seed)` returns a Generator object. Same seed → same draws, every time. The legacy `np.random.seed(...)` global is fine for scripts but `default_rng` is the modern, thread-safe API — use it.\n\n**Example.**\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n# Two researchers, same seed, must get the same sample.\nalice = np.random.default_rng(42).normal(size=3)\nbob   = np.random.default_rng(42).normal(size=3)\nprint(''alice:'', alice)\nprint(''bob:  '', bob)\nprint(''identical:'', np.array_equal(alice, bob))\n```\n\n**Your turn.** Replace `___` so both generators draw the same sequence.\n\n**Expected.** `alice: [ 0.30471708 -1.03998411  0.7504512 ] · bob:   [ 0.30471708 -1.03998411  0.7504512 ] · identical: True`',
