  E'**Concept.** An annual-coupon bond''s fair price is `sum(c / (1+r)**t for t in 1..N) + face / (1+r)**N`. The YTM is the rate `r` that makes this equation balance against the market price. `scipy.optimize.brentq(f, lo, hi)` does a robust bisection — needs `f(lo)` and `f(hi)` to straddle zero. A 0.0001..0.50 bracket covers any realistic bond. At par (price == face), YTM exactly equals the coupon rate — your cheapest sanity check.\n\n**Implement the function.** Implement `ytm`. Define the NPV closure that returns PV minus price; root-find with brentq on (0.0001, 0.5). The docstring spells out both steps.\n\n**Expected.** All tests pass.',
